     "title": "OpenAI is giving ChatGPT free users unlimited text chats",
     "url": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/976239/openai-chatgpt-free-go-text-chats",
     "time": "08-07 02:15",
     "ts": 1786040141,
     "summary": "OpenAI is making a big change for ChatGPT users on its free and Go tiers: Starting next week, users on those tiers will be able to have unlimited text chats wit",
     "source": "The Verge AI",
     "content": "OpenAI is making a big change for ChatGPT users on its free and Go tiers: Starting next week, users on those tiers will be able to have unlimited text chats with the chatbot, according to OpenAI. Right now, you may run into rate limits if you do too many text chats on those tiers, but those limits, just for text, will be going away soon. Messages that include things like file uploads and images will continue to have limits.\nOpenAI is giving ChatGPT free users unlimited text chats\nChatGPT’s GPT-5.6 Sol model will also be ‘more reliable with facts’ for Plus and Pro users.\nChatGPT’s GPT-5.6 Sol model will also be ‘more reliable with facts’ for Plus and Pro users.\nNext week, OpenAI is also adding a “Think” button for free and Go users that they can use to “access higher reasoning for harder questions.” This week, for those users, the company is additionally upgrading ChatGPT’s default AI model to the recently released GPT-5.6 Luna.\nFor Plus and Pro subscribers, GPT-5.6 Sol in ChatGPT is being updated to be “more reliable with facts,” OpenAI says. “The new GPT‑5.6 Sol is designed to make fewer mistakes — especially when answers depend on dates, numbers, sources, rules, or assumptions — by better using the sources it finds to answer your question.” The updated GPT-5.6 Sol will also give you “more direct responses” with “tighter formatting,” and OpenAI says ChatGPT will “avoid extra detail when it does not help.”\nPlus and Pro subscribers can also use a new slider to decide “how much thought ChatGPT puts into an answer.” Both the updated GPT-5.6 Sol and the slider will be available starting Thursday.\nMost Popular\n- Ford’s first ultra-cheap EV is called Fathom, a full-featured truck for $28,350\n- AI bots started a religion — humans immediately followed\n- The messy politics behind Google’s big AI shakeup\n- Jony Ive’s first OpenAI gadget is reportedly a hockey puck-sized smart speaker\n- GTA VI is getting an ‘extended look’ at the end of August",
     "_extract_method": "trafilatura",
     "zh": "OpenAI向ChatGPT免费用户开放无限文本对话",
     "content_zh": "OpenAI宣布，下周起ChatGPT免费及Go层级用户可享受无限文本对话权限，此前该层级用户有文本对话频率限制，含文件上传、图片的消息仍受限。同时免费及Go用户将新增“思考”按钮以应对复杂问题，默认AI模型升级为最新发布的GPT-5.6 Luna；Plus及Pro订阅用户的GPT-5.6 Sol模型将优化事实可靠性，减少日期、数字、来源等维度的错误。"
